# Tate's abstract residue and cotrace–residue identities

Definition: `AlgebraicCurve_TateResidueCurrency` (`35d75f9d-aa25-58cf-9143-abc1acade7fe`), by
Claude, 2026-09-05.

Throughout, a `Place` of an extension $F/K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of
$K$, proper in $F$ and a principal ideal ring, hence a discrete valuation ring, with associated
order function `ord`, residue field and uniformizer.

The first group of definitions sets up Tate's construction over a base field $K$. For a $K$-linear
endomorphism $\varphi$ of a $K$-vector space whose image is finite dimensional, `finrankTrace` is
the trace of $\varphi$ restricted to $\operatorname{range}\varphi$. For three endomorphisms,
`tateComm pA φ ψ` is the composite $p_A\varphi p_A\psi - p_A\psi p_A\varphi$ (in diagrammatic order
as written); its values lie in $\operatorname{range} p_A$, it is antisymmetric in $\varphi,\psi$,
and `tateCommRestrict` is the induced endomorphism of $\operatorname{range} p_A$, whose
`finrankTrace` is `tateCommTrace`. When $\varphi\psi=\psi\varphi$, `tateComm_eq_of_commute` rewrites
the commutator as $p_A\psi(\varphi a-p_A\varphi a)-p_A\varphi(\psi a-p_A\psi a)$. For a place $u$ of
$L/K$, `adicIntegersKSubmod` is the ring of integers of the completion $\hat L_u$ viewed as a
$K$-submodule, `tateProj` is the projection of $\hat L_u$ onto it along a chosen complement, `lmulK`
is multiplication by an element of $\hat L_u$ as a $K$-endomorphism, and `tateRes u fh gh` is
`tateCommTrace` of the two multiplication operators against this projector, defined when the
relevant range is finite dimensional.

Four `Prop`-valued predicates record the expected properties: `KwF4gRRTateCommFinite` (that
finiteness always holds), `KwF4gRRTateAgreement` (`tateRes` against a uniformizer equals the
$K$-trace from the residue field of `kwHgfV352LocalResidueCompletion`, the local residue of an
integral approximant of an element of the completion), `KwF4gRRTateChainRule` (replacing a
uniformizer pulled back from $E$ by the uniformizer at $w$ at the cost of multiplying by the
differential coefficient of the pullback of $v$'s $\mathrm{d}$-coordinate), and
`KwF4gRRTateTraceCompat` (compatibility with `kwHgfV352CompletionTraceAt`, the local trace of $g\in
F$ at $w\mid v$ read in $\hat E_v$).

The remaining predicates concern Kähler differentials: `kaehlerPullback` and `kaehlerCotrace` are
`KaehlerDifferential.map K K E F` applied to an element, resp. as an $E$-linear map
$\Omega_{E/K}\to\Omega_{F/K}$; `Place.regularSubmodule w ωF` is the $K$-submodule of $f\in F$ with
$f\cdot w.\mathrm{differentialCoeff}\,\omega_F$ in the valuation ring at $w$.
`KwHgfV352CompletionTraceSum` asserts that the image of $\mathrm{Tr}_{F/E}g$ in $\hat E_v$ is the
sum of the local completion traces over the fibre of $v$; `KwHgfV352R3MPGKPowBasisLocal` asserts the
corresponding residue-term identity for the elements $\theta^j(\pi^{k+1})^{-1}$ of a local power
basis, and `KwF4R1V391aResidueTraceCompletionCommute` the same identity for arbitrary $g\in F$ with
$\omega_E=v.\mathrm{dCoord}$. Finally `FiberKaehlerCotraceResidueIdentityK` asserts that, given
canonical local residue data at each place of $F$ and a nonzero $\omega_E$ with nonzero pullback,
there is a family of such data at the places of $E$ for which the sum of residue terms over the
fibre of $v$ equals the residue term of $\omega_E$ at the trace $\mathrm{Tr}_{F/E}f$;
`CotraceResidueIdentityOnFiberLocalizedK` is the variant restricted to those $p\in F$ failing to lie
in `regularSubmodule` at at most one place of the fibre.

**Relation to Mathlib.** The trace, the module of Kähler differentials and the functoriality map
`KaehlerDifferential.map` are Mathlib's; `Place`, the places' completions and all residue notions,
as well as Tate's commutator residue, are the project's own.

**Where it is used.** These definitions organise the proof of the residue theorem for function
fields along Tate's route, which underlies the Riemann–Roch theory used for modular curves and their
Jacobians in the Frey curve argument.

